  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have completed the LinguaLive speech translation application, focusing on a clean, minimal, and highly functional experience:\n\n- **Flat, Uncluttered Interface**: Built with a calm off-white base and a subtle emerald accent, entirely removing heavy gradients, dropshadows, or rounded bubbles. The design emphasizes generous whitespace and utilizes a high-contrast layout paired with the `Inter` typeface for maximum legibility.\n- **Real-Time Pairing Engine**: Implemented a WebSocket-based pairing system. Users can instantly start or join calls using a generated 6-character session code or by directly scanning an auto-generated QR code on the start screen.\n- **Push-to-Talk Translation**: Integrated the Web Speech API and the server-side Gemini 3.5 Flash model. As one user holds the microphone to speak, the transcript is translated and broadcast instantly. \n- **Distinguished Transcript Feed**: The live chat feed cleanly delineates original text from the translated text, utilizing subtle opacity pulsing during loading states instead of playful bounce animations. The translated audio is then synthesized and played on the recipient\'s device. \n\nThe application is deployed with the custom Express server backend to securely handle the WebSockets and Gemini API proxy routes."
