steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1783644377
      nanos: 670036738
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Build a web app called \"LinguaLive\" \342\200\224 a live speech translation app for two \npeople speaking different languages. No login required.\n\nSCREENS:\n\n1. Home screen\n   - App name/logo, minimal and centered\n   - Two large buttons: \"Start a call\" and \"Join a call\"\n   - Language selector (dropdown or searchable list) \342\200\224 support at least \n     Hungarian, Persian, English, German, Spanish\n   - Clean, generous whitespace, no clutter\n\n2. Start call screen (after tapping \"Start a call\")\n   - Generate a random 6-character session code\n   - Display a QR code (large, centered) that encodes a join link\n   - Show the code as text below the QR code for manual entry\n   - Show selected language clearly\n   - A subtle \"waiting for the other person to join...\" state with a soft \n     pulsing animation\n   - A cancel/back button\n\n3. Join call screen\n   - \"Scan QR to join\" as the primary action \342\200\224 opens the device camera \n     directly, scanning frame overlaid on the live camera feed\n   - A secondary \"enter code manually\" link/toggle for when scanning isn\'t \n     possible\n   - Language selector for this device\n   - \"Join\" button, disabled until a valid code is entered or scanned\n\n4. Call screen (once paired)\n   - Large circular microphone button, center of screen, tap to talk \n     (push-to-talk style) \342\200\224 this is the main focus of the screen\n   - Visual state changes: idle / listening / translating / speaking \342\200\224 \n     each with a distinct subtle animation or color shift, not text-heavy\n   - No transcript or chat feed visible by default \342\200\224 the screen stays \n     clean and focused on the mic button\n   - A small \"translation chat\" button/icon (e.g. bottom corner or top bar) \n     that opens a panel or overlay showing the live transcript of both \n     languages (original text + translated text, clearly distinguished) \342\200\224 \n     only visible when the user taps this button\n   - Small \"end call\" button\n\nDESIGN DIRECTION \342\200\224 premium, minimal:\n- Flat design, no gradients, no drop shadows, no skeuomorphism\n- Generous whitespace, calm and uncluttered layouts\n- Neutral base palette (off-white / near-black) with a single accent color \n  used sparingly for primary actions and active states\n- Clean sans-serif typography, clear size hierarchy, no more than 2 font \n  weights\n- Rounded corners, consistent and subtle (not overly rounded/bubbly)\n- Smooth, understated micro-animations for state changes \342\200\224 nothing bouncy \n  or playful\n- Mobile-first responsive layout, since this will primarily be used on phones\n- Avoid generic AI-app look: no purple-blue gradient hero sections, no stock \n  illustration graphics, no emoji icons\n\nUse Gemini API for translation and speech features if natively supported. \nDo not build the peer-to-peer audio connection or backend signaling server \nyet \342\200\224 just build the UI flow and screen states with placeholder/mock data \nfor now."
    items {
      text: "Build a web app called \"LinguaLive\" \342\200\224 a live speech translation app for two \npeople speaking different languages. No login required.\n\nSCREENS:\n\n1. Home screen\n   - App name/logo, minimal and centered\n   - Two large buttons: \"Start a call\" and \"Join a call\"\n   - Language selector (dropdown or searchable list) \342\200\224 support at least \n     Hungarian, Persian, English, German, Spanish\n   - Clean, generous whitespace, no clutter\n\n2. Start call screen (after tapping \"Start a call\")\n   - Generate a random 6-character session code\n   - Display a QR code (large, centered) that encodes a join link\n   - Show the code as text below the QR code for manual entry\n   - Show selected language clearly\n   - A subtle \"waiting for the other person to join...\" state with a soft \n     pulsing animation\n   - A cancel/back button\n\n3. Join call screen\n   - \"Scan QR to join\" as the primary action \342\200\224 opens the device camera \n     directly, scanning frame overlaid on the live camera feed\n   - A secondary \"enter code manually\" link/toggle for when scanning isn\'t \n     possible\n   - Language selector for this device\n   - \"Join\" button, disabled until a valid code is entered or scanned\n\n4. Call screen (once paired)\n   - Large circular microphone button, center of screen, tap to talk \n     (push-to-talk style) \342\200\224 this is the main focus of the screen\n   - Visual state changes: idle / listening / translating / speaking \342\200\224 \n     each with a distinct subtle animation or color shift, not text-heavy\n   - No transcript or chat feed visible by default \342\200\224 the screen stays \n     clean and focused on the mic button\n   - A small \"translation chat\" button/icon (e.g. bottom corner or top bar) \n     that opens a panel or overlay showing the live transcript of both \n     languages (original text + translated text, clearly distinguished) \342\200\224 \n     only visible when the user taps this button\n   - Small \"end call\" button\n\nDESIGN DIRECTION \342\200\224 premium, minimal:\n- Flat design, no gradients, no drop shadows, no skeuomorphism\n- Generous whitespace, calm and uncluttered layouts\n- Neutral base palette (off-white / near-black) with a single accent color \n  used sparingly for primary actions and active states\n- Clean sans-serif typography, clear size hierarchy, no more than 2 font \n  weights\n- Rounded corners, consistent and subtle (not overly rounded/bubbly)\n- Smooth, understated micro-animations for state changes \342\200\224 nothing bouncy \n  or playful\n- Mobile-first responsive layout, since this will primarily be used on phones\n- Avoid generic AI-app look: no purple-blue gradient hero sections, no stock \n  illustration graphics, no emoji icons\n\nUse Gemini API for translation and speech features if natively supported. \nDo not build the peer-to-peer audio connection or backend signaling server \nyet \342\200\224 just build the UI flow and screen states with placeholder/mock data \nfor now."
    }
  }
}
