  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I\'ve identified and fixed the root causes that were preventing the translated voice from playing on the receiving device. There were two underlying issues:\n\n1. **Incorrect Language Code Format**: The browser\'s Text-to-Speech (TTS) engine requires a strict BCP-47 language tag (e.g., `\"es-ES\"` for Spanish, `\"de-DE\"` for German). The app was accidentally sending the literal language name (e.g., `\"Spanish\"`), which caused the browser to silently fail to find a matching voice. I\'ve updated the logic to ensure the correct standard codes are used.\n2. **Mobile Browser Audio Restrictions**: Mobile browsers (especially iOS Safari) strictly block speech synthesis from playing in the background unless it has been explicitly \"unlocked\" by a direct user interaction. I\'ve added a silent \"warm-up\" mechanism that initializes the speech engine the moment you tap **Start a call** or **Join a call**, ensuring the device is granted permission to play the translated audio when it arrives.\n\nThe dev server has been restarted with these fixes. Give it another try, and the receiving device should now correctly speak the translated responses out loud!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
