  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Envisioning UI Overhaul**\n\nI\'m focusing on the UI redesign, aiming for a premium, walkie-talkie aesthetic. Right now, I\'m leaning heavily towards dark mode or dark accents to convey a tactical feel, perhaps using dark gray or near-black backgrounds like `bg-zinc-900`. I\'m also considering incorporating matte textures to enhance the overall impression of quality.\n\n\n**Refining Color and Style**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the color palette and overall style. I\'ve decided to go with a very dark charcoal/black base (like `bg-zinc-950`) for a premium feel. The key element will be a bright accent color, perhaps orange or neon green, reserved primarily for the active state and push-to-talk button. I\'m also ensuring clean, monospaced typography for technical details. I\'m sticking to a flat, high-contrast design, no gradients or drop shadows. I\'ve updated the global theme with dark mode in `index.css`.\n\n\n**Implementing Dark Theme Styling**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in implementing the dark theme styling across all components. I\'ve updated `index.css` with a very dark gray background and white text. I\'m focusing on components now, like `Home.tsx`, `StartCall.tsx`, `JoinCall.tsx`, and especially `CallRoom.tsx`. The core `CallRoom.tsx` component will have a large central button with an accent color, like orange or amber, with \"Push to talk\" text and other technical indicators, and a flat design. I\'m leveraging Tailwind classes throughout.\n\n\n**Defining Component Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now diving into specific component styling. I\'ve decided on an orange active state, (`bg-orange-500 text-black`), with a secondary, `bg-zinc-800 text-white`. I\'ve set the background to dark gray, with white text for the QR code, with a white background and black foreground. I\'ve designed the input field in `JoinCall.tsx` to have a `bg-zinc-800` background. In `CallRoom.tsx`, I am working on the huge, rounded PTT button, which should be orange when idle, and red when transmitting, with \"TRANSMITTING\", \"RECEIVING\", and \"STANDBY\" state texts. I\'m imagining a dark, sliding transcript overlay as well.\n\n\n**Adjusting Typography and Elements**\n\nI\'m now changing the font in `globals.css` to use \"Inter\" as the primary font and \"JetBrains Mono\" for monospace elements. In `Home.tsx`, I\'ve adjusted the title to uppercase, bold white text, and changed the subtitle to uppercase, tracking-widest text in a gray color with monospace typography. This enhances the overall tactical appearance.\n\n\n**Refining Element Styling**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on styling form elements. I\'ve adjusted the select dropdown in `Home.tsx` to match the dark theme, using dark gray with a white border and focus effect. For the buttons, I\'m ensuring a clean transition on hover and making sure they reflect the active and inactive states. I will be adjusting the appearance of the button states in `Home.tsx`.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 712751732
    }
