  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Language Support**\n\nI\'ve realized that while common languages like English and Spanish are generally safe bets for text-to-speech, less common locales such as Farsi (`fa-IR`) and Hungarian (`hu-HU`) might not be universally supported across all devices, particularly on iOS where native voices can vary with the operating system version. Now I need to check the code that implements TTS for locales!\n\n\n**Analyzing Language Flow**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the language flow in the application. I see that if there are other users in the room, the target language defaults to the first user\'s preference. This is followed correctly by message translation and dispatch. The receiver uses their own language.bcp47 for the text-to-speech. I\'m now considering edge cases related to socket re-connection and empty room language configurations.\n\n\n**Addressing Socket Reconnects**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the critical issue of socket reconnection within the `CallRoom.tsx` component. The absence of a `join_room` emit on reconnect is the root cause; users are silently dropped from the room\'s language configuration. To remedy this, I\'m proposing a straightforward fix: emitting `join_room` within `CallRoom.tsx` itself, specifically on component mount and on socket reconnect to maintain room state.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 153300160
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
