    thinking: "**Defining User Input**\n\nI\'m focusing on incorporating a user name input field. This entails adding a mechanism for the user to specify their name, likely on the home screen, before a call. Then, I need to seamlessly integrate this name into the chat or call room display.\n\n\n**Analyzing Speaker Identities**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the current application state. Right now, `App.tsx` handles language and room code, and `Home.tsx` has language selection and call buttons. The `CallRoom.tsx` uses a random `myId` and `speakerId`, but displays messages as \"isMe ? originalText : translatedText,\" and lacks speaker names. I\'ve realized I need to pass the `userName` from `Home` through to `CallRoom` by updating the state in `App.tsx`. I think I will add a `userName` text input to `Home.tsx` and a `speakerName` string to the `Message` interface, in `src/types.ts`.\n\n\n**Refining UI Integration**\n\nI\'m now focused on integrating the user\'s name throughout the application. I\'m adding a `name` state and text input to `Home.tsx` to collect user input, ensuring the buttons are disabled if the name is empty. I\'m updating `onStartCall` and `onJoinCall` prop types. Also, I need to ensure the server updates the `speech_ended` listener to receive the `speakerName`. I am handling cases where users join via URL, and updating the state management accordingly.\n\n\n**Implementing Server Updates**\n\nI\'m currently updating the server to handle speaker names correctly. I\'ve ensured `speakerName` is included when emitting \"new\\_message.\" I\'m also preparing to pass `userName` to `CallRoom.tsx` as a prop and use it to populate the `speakerName` when a speech ends. I am implementing UI updates, so the chat UI displays the speaker name above the message bubbles.\n\n\n**Integrating User Input**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user name throughout the application and I have updated prop types for `Home.tsx` to handle the user\'s name. I\'m adding `name` state and a text input field to `Home.tsx` so the user can input their name. I\'m updating `onStartCall` and `onJoinCall` prop types to accept the name. Also, I\'m ensuring the server updates the `speech_ended` listener. Finally, the server will correctly emit speaker name.\n\n\n**Updating CallRoom Logic**\n\nI\'m now focused on the CallRoom and making updates there. I\'ve added `userName: string` to `CallRoomProps` in `/src/components/CallRoom.tsx`. When emitting `speech_ended`, I\'ve made sure to include `speakerName: userName`. Additionally, I\'m updating the transcript UI so that it shows the speaker\'s name, or \"You\" for the local user. The UI now displays the speaker name or \"Stranger\" if the name isn\'t available, or \"You\" if the message is from me.\n\n\n**Enhancing UI Presentation**\n\nI\'m now integrating the user\'s name throughout the application. I am now updating the UI. I\'ve considered how the display of messages and names in `CallRoom` can be enhanced. It includes adding the user name above messages in the transcript, especially in the walkie-talkie style interface. I\'m focusing on UI elements to clearly identify the speaker. I\'m taking into consideration the real-time \"who is speaking\" element.\n\n\n"
